<title>SWEDEN: ABB sets up fund to invest in east Europe.</title>
<headline>ABB sets up fund to invest in east Europe.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish-Swiss engineering group ABB said on Friday its investment management unit will set up a guarantee fund on February 3 that will invest in central and east European share markets.</p>
<p>The closed-end Luxemburg registered fund will guarantee pay-back of invested capital after five years. Then it will be converted to an open fund.</p>
<p>The fund will invest in options and share derivatives. Part of the portfolio will be invested in zero-coupon bonds, to ensure the guaranteed pay-back.</p>
<p>Furthermore, the fund has an insurance guarantee issued by ABB owned insurer Sirius International Insurance Corp.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1006</p>
